  <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
  <h3>Does GEO replace SEO?</h3>
  <p>No. GEO depends on good technical SEO because models still need to discover, fetch, parse, and attribute pages. GEO extends the system from document discovery into entity clarity and evidence resolution.</p>
  <h3>Can structured data guarantee an AI citation?</h3>
  <p>No. Structured data supplies explicit clues; it does not guarantee ranking, inclusion, or citation. The page must still be useful, visible, accurate, and supported by a credible information environment.</p>
  <h3>What is the first GEO improvement to make?</h3>
  <p>Start with one important entity and one query set. Align the page title, visible definition, author, canonical URL, JSON-LD, internal links, external evidence, and image alt text around the same clear answer.</p>
